  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.29",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $\\Sigma$ be a locally flat surface in $S^{4}$ with $\\pi_{1}(S^{4} \\setminus \\Sigma)$ cyclic.\n\n(a) Prove that $\\Sigma$ is topologically unknotted.\n\n(b) Assuming that $\\Sigma$ is smoothly embedded and orientable, prove that $\\Sigma$ is smoothly unknotted (or find an example that is not).",
